WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:01.298
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.298 --> 00:00:04.597
Today's message is follow your heart.

00:00:04.597 --> 00:00:07.097
Over to you, Shaquille O'Neal.

00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:10.971
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:10.971 --> 00:00:13.642
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.642 --> 00:00:17.798
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.798 --> 00:00:20.367
- What is it about investment
and entrepreneurship

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:23.023
that sort of has bitten you?

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:26.636
- I never look at it as
investments, believe it or not.

00:00:26.636 --> 00:00:29.526
I just look at it as partnerships,

00:00:29.526 --> 00:00:31.251
help changing the world,

00:00:31.251 --> 00:00:34.499
and just being part of
something that's inspiring.

00:00:34.499 --> 00:00:35.742
My business people, all the time,

00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:36.777
whenever they talk about money,

00:00:36.777 --> 00:00:38.453
you can ask them, I'm like, ah,

00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:39.286
I don't want to hear it.

00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:42.066
But if they bring an idea to me

00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:44.217
that I think is going
to go to the next level,

00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.638
most of the time if I follow my heart,

00:00:46.638 --> 00:00:48.083
then everything else will fall into place.

00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:49.676
I've never ever done a deal,

00:00:49.676 --> 00:00:51.389
eh, we've got this suit company,

00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:52.985
we throw some pinstripes in the suit,

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:55.977
you give me 100,000, we
sell 20 of them, we make.

00:00:55.977 --> 00:00:58.635
I've never did a deal where
it was always based on money.

00:00:58.635 --> 00:01:01.336
I always did my business
deals based on how I felt

00:01:01.336 --> 00:01:02.830
it was going to go in the future,

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.975
how I felt it was going to
help and inspire somebody.

00:01:05.975 --> 00:01:08.022
- If you are starting a business
just trying to make money,

00:01:08.022 --> 00:01:09.003
you're going to lose.

00:01:09.003 --> 00:01:10.971
This is how so many
people go out of business.

00:01:10.971 --> 00:01:13.570
They read the magazine of
the 100 hottest startups

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.338
to start this year, and
they try them and they fail.

00:01:16.338 --> 00:01:17.173
You lose.

00:01:17.173 --> 00:01:19.664
I don't know how many times
you need to hear this message.

00:01:19.664 --> 00:01:21.415
I don't know how many
times we have profiled

00:01:21.415 --> 00:01:23.892
different successful people.

00:01:23.892 --> 00:01:26.244
I think this channel,

00:01:26.244 --> 00:01:27.828
we've profiled more successful people

00:01:27.828 --> 00:01:29.828
than maybe anybody else,

00:01:31.372 --> 00:01:33.732
maybe any other YouTube channel,

00:01:33.732 --> 00:01:37.276
maybe any other publication, period.

00:01:37.276 --> 00:01:38.275
Maybe.

00:01:38.275 --> 00:01:40.662
If we're not there, we're in the top.

00:01:40.662 --> 00:01:44.284
From athletes to musicians to
entrepreneurs to politicians

00:01:44.284 --> 00:01:48.169
to inventors to artists
all over the world,

00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:50.354
people from different
countries, different cultures,

00:01:50.354 --> 00:01:53.053
different races, different genders,

00:01:53.053 --> 00:01:55.491
and the single most consistent thing

00:01:55.491 --> 00:01:59.516
that everybody says is you
have to follow your heart.

00:01:59.516 --> 00:02:01.945
You have to have passion for
the work that you're doing.

00:02:01.945 --> 00:02:03.443
I don't know how many
times you need to hear it.

00:02:03.443 --> 00:02:04.556
I don't know that,

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:05.627
we're making another video on it.

00:02:05.627 --> 00:02:07.324
A lot of you guys are going to get it.

00:02:07.324 --> 00:02:08.929
A lot of you guys still won't get it.

00:02:08.929 --> 00:02:12.044
Hopefully by hearing it from
Shaquille O'Neal this time

00:02:12.044 --> 00:02:13.141
and different entrepreneurs,

00:02:13.141 --> 00:02:15.486
at some point it's going to sink in.

00:02:15.486 --> 00:02:17.018
If the only reason that
you're doing something

00:02:17.018 --> 00:02:18.028
is just for the money,

00:02:18.028 --> 00:02:19.534
you will always live paycheck to paycheck

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:22.461
'cause there's nothing
deeper driving you forward.

00:02:22.461 --> 00:02:24.043
As soon as you get enough
money to pay your bills,

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:24.876
you're going to ease up the throttle

00:02:24.876 --> 00:02:26.825
and you won't have any success,

00:02:26.825 --> 00:02:28.364
where if you're driven by something

00:02:28.364 --> 00:02:29.664
more than just making money

00:02:29.664 --> 00:02:30.874
and making money is important.

00:02:30.874 --> 00:02:32.098
Listen, we're running a business.

00:02:32.098 --> 00:02:33.078
You got to make money.

00:02:33.078 --> 00:02:34.585
Money provides for a
lot of amazing things.

00:02:34.585 --> 00:02:36.291
It's not that money is evil.

00:02:36.291 --> 00:02:38.538
There just has to be
something above money,

00:02:38.538 --> 00:02:40.033
something driving you.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.194
Look at whoever you look up to most.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:44.703
Whoever has the most
success in your industry,

00:02:44.703 --> 00:02:48.148
they wanted to change the
way something was done.

00:02:48.148 --> 00:02:49.411
They had this thing inside them

00:02:49.411 --> 00:02:51.478
that they had to get out,

00:02:51.478 --> 00:02:54.325
and they made a lot of money
in the process of doing it.

00:02:54.325 --> 00:02:56.136
But money was never the number one goal.

00:02:56.136 --> 00:02:57.303
It never is.

00:02:57.303 --> 00:03:00.943
And so, I hope that by
hearing the message again,

00:03:00.943 --> 00:03:02.519
for some of you, it's going to sink in,

00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:05.068
and this is going to be the
time that you actually decide

00:03:05.068 --> 00:03:07.325
to do the thing that
you're passionate about

00:03:07.325 --> 00:03:09.607
because I don't want you wasting time.

00:03:09.607 --> 00:03:11.113
I don't want you just
wanting to be an entrepreneur

00:03:11.113 --> 00:03:13.534
'cause you want the
entrepreneur lifestyle.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.040
I want you to do something important.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.266
And it's only going to
come by leaning in heavily

00:03:17.266 --> 00:03:19.141
on the thing that you are
most passionate about.

00:03:19.141 --> 00:03:20.500
So, the question of the day today is

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.594
I'm curious, who is the
most successful person

00:03:22.594 --> 00:03:25.697
that you look up to
that really exemplifies

00:03:25.697 --> 00:03:28.519
that characteristic of
just loving what they do

00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:31.319
and put in the hustle,
hard work, and effort?

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:32.802
Who is that person for you?

00:03:32.802 --> 00:03:33.944
Super curious to find out.

00:03:33.944 --> 00:03:35.329
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:03:35.329 --> 00:03:37.157
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Michael Brown.

00:03:37.157 --> 00:03:38.828
Michael, thank you so
much for picking up a copy

00:03:38.828 --> 00:03:40.690
of my book, Your One Word.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.903
It really means a lot to me, man,

00:03:41.903 --> 00:03:43.729
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:43.729 --> 00:03:44.819
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:46.753
I hope you have an amazing day.

00:03:46.753 --> 00:03:47.621
I believe in you

00:03:47.621 --> 00:03:49.879
and hope you continue
to believe in yourself.

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:51.243
And I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:03:51.243 --> 00:03:53.867
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.192
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:56.192 --> 00:03:59.609
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:04:01.596 --> 00:04:05.793
- The last Rocky movie before
Creed, the final scene,

00:04:05.793 --> 00:04:09.392
was it your way of saying
goodbye to the character,

00:04:09.392 --> 00:04:10.394
goodbye to that?

00:04:10.394 --> 00:04:12.097
- Yeah, goodbye to everything,

00:04:12.097 --> 00:04:14.486
goodbye to the best chapters of my life,

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:15.827
at least professional life.

00:04:15.827 --> 00:04:16.897
It really was.

00:04:16.897 --> 00:04:20.904
Then, along comes this
young guy to Oakland

00:04:20.904 --> 00:04:22.218
and I'm going, what?

00:04:22.218 --> 00:04:23.281
- Ryan Coogler.

00:04:23.281 --> 00:04:24.604
- Ryan Coogler.

00:04:24.604 --> 00:04:25.816
- [Robin] When director Ryan Coogler

00:04:25.816 --> 00:04:27.254
first met with Stallone,

00:04:27.254 --> 00:04:29.705
he was untested as a feature filmmaker,

00:04:29.705 --> 00:04:31.851
but he had an intensely personal idea

00:04:31.851 --> 00:04:34.315
for reviving the Rocky franchise.

00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:37.885
Coogler's father had fallen
gravely ill a few years earlier.

00:04:37.885 --> 00:04:39.703
With Ryan by his side,

00:04:39.703 --> 00:04:43.350
there was only one thing the
elder Coogler wanted to watch.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.733
- The father is a very
soulful powerful man,

00:04:46.733 --> 00:04:49.976
and now, he's being reduced
to a shell of his former self.

00:04:49.976 --> 00:04:54.890
But oddly, he watches Rocky
again and again and again.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.311
This son, who loves his father,

00:04:56.311 --> 00:04:57.383
sitting right beside him,

00:04:57.383 --> 00:04:58.436
and he's watching his father

00:04:58.436 --> 00:05:00.265
disintegrate before his very eyes,

00:05:00.265 --> 00:05:04.262
the traumatic impact was so
imprinted on this young man

00:05:04.262 --> 00:05:06.090
that he never got over it.

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.309
So, he comes to me and he goes,

00:05:07.309 --> 00:05:08.336
"Hey, look at this great idea.

00:05:08.336 --> 00:05:10.661
"I'm going to revive Rocky."

00:05:10.661 --> 00:05:11.653
I go, "How?"

00:05:11.653 --> 00:05:12.673
And when he told me his story,

00:05:12.673 --> 00:05:15.093
I said, "This is insane, wrong."

00:05:15.093 --> 00:05:16.522
You're a young kid.

00:05:16.522 --> 00:05:18.028
You haven't done anything yet,

00:05:18.028 --> 00:05:19.987
but I appreciate the thought.

00:05:19.987 --> 00:05:21.668
He goes, "Okay, see you around."

00:05:21.668 --> 00:05:23.279
And he goes out and he does a masterpiece,

00:05:23.279 --> 00:05:25.478
Fruitvale Station, wins
the Cannes Film Festival.

00:05:25.478 --> 00:05:26.683
Every studio wants him.

00:05:26.683 --> 00:05:27.606
What's he want to do?

00:05:27.606 --> 00:05:28.439
Creed.

00:05:28.439 --> 00:05:31.411
I went, now, either this guy here is just

00:05:31.411 --> 00:05:35.578
trying my patience or he reminds
me of a guy I used to know.

00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:38.195
- I was going to say,

00:05:38.195 --> 00:05:40.151
that was you 40 years ago.

00:05:40.151 --> 00:05:41.989
- Yeah, it was.

00:05:41.989 --> 00:05:43.010
Absolutely.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.471
Then, I realized this
is not a movie for him.

00:05:45.471 --> 00:05:47.413
It's for his father.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.916
This is all about a love
letter to his father.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:52.205
- Now, if you really dug down deep

00:05:52.205 --> 00:05:55.242
and ask a real Rocky fan
why he likes the movies,

00:05:55.242 --> 00:05:56.498
it's usually because they watched them

00:05:56.498 --> 00:05:57.681
with someone that they loved.

00:05:57.681 --> 00:05:58.621
What's so great about them

00:05:58.621 --> 00:06:00.344
is they're so personal to people.

00:06:00.344 --> 00:06:02.563
People just associate
them with their family.

00:06:02.563 --> 00:06:03.794
- [Narrator] This young, dedicated artist

00:06:03.794 --> 00:06:07.173
can't help but reflect on
those who once doubted him.

00:06:07.173 --> 00:06:09.193
- They never said I
wasn't talented enough.

00:06:09.193 --> 00:06:11.430
They'll say something like,
"The industry is shady.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.831
"You don't need to be doing this."

00:06:12.831 --> 00:06:14.206
I respect their opinions,

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.105
but at the end of the day,
I had to follow my heart

00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:17.052
and that's what I wanted to do.

00:06:17.052 --> 00:06:18.095
It was a passion.

00:06:18.095 --> 00:06:19.470
I couldn't shake it.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.489
And I'd be hurt now if
I didn't stick with it

00:06:21.489 --> 00:06:24.173
'cause it'd always be in my head.

00:06:24.173 --> 00:06:27.461
- And Paul, when you first
signed up for the first one,

00:06:27.461 --> 00:06:30.050
which was back in '99, 2000,

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:33.295
did you think you'd be
sitting here in 2013,

00:06:33.295 --> 00:06:34.931
talking about number six?

00:06:34.931 --> 00:06:36.735
- No, not a chance.

00:06:36.735 --> 00:06:38.636
No screenplay, nothing, when I signed on.

00:06:38.636 --> 00:06:40.281
It was just an idea.

00:06:40.281 --> 00:06:42.598
And it was funny because
I wanted to do it,

00:06:42.598 --> 00:06:43.727
working with my friends

00:06:43.727 --> 00:06:45.628
'cause I'd already worked
with these people before.

00:06:45.628 --> 00:06:46.888
And they're like, "You can't do it."

00:06:46.888 --> 00:06:48.571
My representatives were
telling me, "You can't do it."

00:06:48.571 --> 00:06:49.512
There's no script.

00:06:49.512 --> 00:06:51.159
There's nothing.
- That's really funny.

00:06:51.159 --> 00:06:52.231
- You didn't listen to their advice?

00:06:52.231 --> 00:06:53.064
- You were right.

00:06:53.064 --> 00:06:53.927
- I got lucky.

00:06:53.927 --> 00:06:55.827
But it was just following
your heart kind of thing,

00:06:55.827 --> 00:06:58.354
and it wasn't even about down the road.

00:06:58.354 --> 00:07:00.533
It was about living in
the moment and got lucky.

